  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bfcb709b487afd749b8fbd2c4c50e261, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cultist
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: CardDungeon::Assets.Scripts.Heroes.HeroSO
  Key: Cultist
  Label: Cultist
  Blurb: Speaks to things that should not answer. They answer.
  Vision:
    Fantasy: 'An eldritch-horror summoner: he calls things from below the deep to
      fight beside the party, and pays for his rites in his own blood (decided 2026-10-04/05).'
    Role: Summoner and curse-caster. Frail Intelligence/Spirit caster who wants his
      horrors in front of him.
    SignatureMechanic: 'Adding party members mid-fight: horrors that fight beside
      the party (SummonKind.JoinParty).'
    UltraStyle: Rituals
    Ultras:
    - Name: Sacrifice
      Effect: Sacrifice a target party member, replacing him/her with a demon (demon
        scaled off of the sacrificed party member's stats). Always summoned with
        full health, so a good idea to use when a party member is about to die.
      Unlock: In the demon summoner branch
    Branches:
    - GridBranch: a
      Becomes: Eldritch summoner - a bit stronger on its own than a normal branch,
        to justify committing to it.
      IntendedKit: Summon Writhing Spawn => Summon The Watcher => Sacrifice (Ultra,
        Void Shards)
      Summon: Writhing Spawn, The Watcher
    - GridBranch: b
      Becomes: 'Madness: curses that slow, weaken and rot.'
      IntendedKit: Whisper of Madness => Dread => Mind Rot
      Summon: 
    - GridBranch: c
      Becomes: 'Dark rites: the party grows stronger and he pays for it in blood.'
      IntendedKit: Blood Rite => Rite of Warding => Dark Communion
      Summon: 
    Overlaps: 
    OpenQuestions: 'All numbers are first drafts (Claude, 2026-10-05) - stats, abilities,
      summons. Do branches B and C want summons of their own (every branch eventually
      ends in a summon)? More Rituals Ultras? Sacrifice sits at the summoner branch''s
      tip behind 3 Void Shards. Unlock: captive in The Hollow Vault.'
